<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<advancedSettings>
<!--
  Advanced system settings of ESXi hosts to publish (VCF Content Factory vCommunity).

  Name the ESXi advanced options whose value you want on every ESXi host. The
  adapter publishes each one as a property of the host, under the option name
  exactly as ESXi spells it (letters and case matter).

  Format
    - Separate entries with commas. A line break does NOT separate entries:
      two names on two lines with no comma between them are read as one
      name that contains a line break, which is skipped and reported.
    - An XML comment, like this one, is ignored. To switch an entry on, move
      it out of the comment, and keep the comma after it.
    - Do not write two hyphens in a row inside a comment.

  Do not edit this shipped file: a forced upgrade of the pack replaces it and
  your edits are lost. Make a copy under another name in the VCF Operations configuration-file store, and
  enter that name (no .xml) in the account's ESXi Advanced System Settings
  Config File field. As shipped, every entry is commented out, so nothing is collected.

  Examples, one per line:
    Net.TcpipHeapSize,
    Net.TcpipHeapMax,
    Mem.ShareForceSalting,
    UserVars.ESXiShellTimeOut,
    UserVars.SuppressShellWarning,
    Syslog.global.logHost,
    NFS.MaxVolumes,
-->
</advancedSettings>
